Troubleshoot and fix a Docker container crash caused by a missing application dependency.

Requirements:
- Located in `/app`, you will find a `Dockerfile` and `app.py`.
- Build the initial image (`docker build -t myapp-web:latest /app`) and run it (`docker run myapp-web:latest`). Observe that the container exits immediately with Exit Code 1.
- Inspect container logs (`docker logs`) to identify the missing dependency (`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'flask'`).
- Update `/app/Dockerfile` to install the required dependency (`RUN pip install flask`).
- Rebuild the image (`docker build -t myapp-web:latest /app`) and run a container (`docker run -d -p 5000:5000 --name web_container myapp-web:latest`).
- Ensure the container remains active in the `running` state and serves HTTP requests.
